Bundled third-party assets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following files are redistributed inside this repository and, where noted,
compiled into the resulting binaries. They keep their own licenses, which are
not MIT and whose attribution requirements must be preserved downstream.

1. Roboto (assets/fonts/Roboto-Regular.ttf, assets/fonts/Roboto-Bold.ttf)
   Copyright the Roboto Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto)
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   Embedded by the `render` crate as the fallback face used to rasterize the
   standard-14 fonts when a PDF does not embed its own font program.
   See assets/fonts/LICENSE.txt.

2. sRGB ICC profile (assets/icc/sRGB.icc)
   sRGB-v2-micro.icc from the Compact ICC Profiles project
   (https://github.com/saucecontrol/Compact-ICC-Profiles).
   Released under CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication).
   Embedded by the `pdf` crate as the PDF/A OutputIntent destination profile.
   See assets/icc/LICENSE.txt.

3. Schibsted Grotesk (site/public/fonts/schibsted-grotesk-latin.woff2)
   Licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Used only by the project
   website, never compiled into the library.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Rust dependencies are fetched from crates.io and are not vendored here. Every
one of them carries a permissive license; the allow-list is enforced in CI by
`cargo deny` (see deny.toml) and the inventory is documented in LICENSES.md.
